graphy/Hash%20Functions/Hash%20Functions/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Introduction</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Introduction&lt;/h1&gt; &lt;p&gt;In practice, it is easier to construct hashing algorithms which operate on relatively small, fixed input lengths, whilst still keeping the ou...&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Cryptography/Hash%20Functions/Merkle-Damg%C3%A5rd%20Transform/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 08:07:27 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/feed_rss_created.xml">Razon</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Cryptography/Hash%20Functions/Merkle-Damg%C3%A5rd%20Transform/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Collisions</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Collisions&lt;/h1&gt; &lt;p&gt;A &lt;em&gt;collision&lt;/em&gt; is a pair of two inputs $x \ne x&#39;$ which produce the same digest when hashed, i.e. $H(x) = H(x&#39;)$.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;When the input space is large...&lt;/p&gt;</description> <link>https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Cryptography/Hash%20Functions/Security%20Definitions/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 08:07:27 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/feed_rss_created.xml">Razon</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Cryptography/Hash%20Functions/Security%20Definitions/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Index</title> <description></description> <link>https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Cryptography/Integrity%20Verification/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 08:07:27 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/feed_rss_created.xml">Razon</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mihailkovachev.github.io/Razon/Computer%20Science/Cryptography/Integrity%20Verification/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Introduction</title> <description>&lt;h1&gt;Introduction&lt;/h1&gt; &lt;p&